      "failure_scenario": "HUDCO improves its net interest margin through better asset quality, lower NPAs, reduced provisioning requirements, or a favourable interest rate cycle, allowing PAT to grow even if revenue stagnates or mildly declines — making the net income forecast significantly too pessimistic.",
      "risk": "High"
    },
    {
      "assumption": "Shares outstanding remain static at approximately 200.19 Cr shares throughout the forecast period, with no dilution or buyback activity.",
      "failure_scenario": "The Government of India or HUDCO management initiates a follow-on public offering (FPO) or rights issue to raise capital for balance sheet expansion, increasing share count and diluting EPS beyond what the model projects, or conversely a buyback boosts EPS above forecasted levels.",
